WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.798
DS-1000 gives the community a data science code
benchmark that is realistic,

00:00:04.878 --> 00:00:08.007
reliably evaluated, and resistant to memorization.

00:00:08.088 --> 00:00:11.602
Because it is built from natural StackOverflow problems,

00:00:11.682 --> 00:00:16.288
judged by executing code against test cases and
surface-form constraints,

00:00:16.368 --> 00:00:21.743
and defended by deliberate perturbation, its scores
are trustworthy and hard to game.

00:00:21.823 --> 00:00:27.007
And because even the strongest model reaches only
forty-three point three percent,

00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:32.270
it makes clear how much room remains for progress
in data science code generation.
